    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "p2p: use header time for compact block recency",
    "user": {
      "login": "xternet",
      "id": 58574501,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTc0NTAx",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58574501?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/xternet",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/xternet",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xternet/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xternet/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xternet/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xternet/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xternet/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xternet/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xternet/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xternet/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xternet/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- use the announced block header's timestamp to check unsolicited compact-block recency\r\n- preserve the existing 20-target-spacing cutoff\r\n- leave `CanDirectFetch()` and its other callers unchanged\r\n- add regression coverage for compact-block relay when the active tip is stale\r\n\r\n`CanDirectFetch()` checks the active tip's timestamp. After 20 target spacings without a block, this causes a recent unsolicited compact block from a high-bandwidth peer to be ignored.\r\n\r\nThis change uses the announced block header's timestamp for that local check instead. Although header timestamps are miner-selected, this only affects whether reconstruction is attempted; existing proof-of-work, chain-work, peer, resource, and block-validation checks still apply.\r\n\r\nFixes #33578\r\n\r\n## Test coverage\r\n\r\nThe functional test keeps the active tip stale and verifies that:\r\n\r\n- an old unsolicited compact block is ignored\r\n- a distinct compact block with a recent header triggers `GETBLOCKTXN`\r\n- mock time is restored after the test\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n`test/functional/p2p_compactblocks.py`\r\n",
